; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
; SELinux module "herkos" (package herkos-selinux).
;
; herkosd starts each tool of a person as a template unit
; (vilna-mcp-*@<uid>.service, herkos/rs/crates/herkosd/src/units.rs). The
; unit's stdin and stdout are a connection to a socket herkosd listens on in
; /run/herkos-tools/<uid>/ (StandardInput=file:). systemd itself (PID 1,
; init_t) opens that connection before the tool starts, and herkosd runs
; unconfined (unconfined_service_t) until it gets a policy of its own
; (item 25 of the alpha plan). Without this rule the policy refuses the
; connection, every tool unit fails with 208/STDIN and Gloxi has no tools
; (found on the image, Build13.2, ADR 0025 step 6).
;
; The socket stays 0600 and owned by herkos, so only root can connect: the
; person's own programs still cannot pose as a tool.
(allow init_t unconfined_service_t (unix_stream_socket (connectto)))
